listitem.para:
@vocab to
                https://www.onvif.org/ver10/agentic/linkml/, so that unqualified terms
              of the Agentic Service bundle expand in the ONVIF vocabulary;

each concrete third-party class used in the envelope as an expanded term
              definition whose @id is that class's CURIE and whose type-scoped
                @context maps every locally declared, unqualified JSON property name to
              its slot_uri. Inherited ONVIF properties continue to use the outer
                @vocab mapping.

section.para:
The id slot is deliberately not bound to the JSON-LD node identifier
        @id. A bare UUID is not an IRI: a JSON-LD processor asked to read it as
        @id would resolve it against a base URI and produce an identifier that means
        nothing. Binding it properly would require every identifier in this model to be written in the
        urn:uuid: form that the paragraph above forbids, on the wire and in every digest
        computed over it, in exchange for a graph structure no part of this specification needs (see
        ).

The two keywords are fields of the envelope and not of the delivery that carried it.
        @context is the inline context derived from the modules represented in the
        payload, as specified in ;
        @type has the value onvif:InformationEnvelope. The envelope
        carries them because it is the outermost object of a payload and nothing encloses it that
        could state what it is.

Both stages are required to establish the integrity and authenticity of the enclosed
            items. An envelope that fails either stage shall be treated as unauthentic as a whole;
            a verifier shall not salvage individual items from it.

